# A16 Self-Hosting Bootstrap Compiler
#
# This directory contains a minimal A16 compiler written in A16 itself.
# It demonstrates that A16 is expressive enough to compile a meaningful
# subset of its own language.
#
# Components:
#   lexer.a16    - Tokenizer (keywords, operators, literals, identifiers)
#   parser.a16   - Recursive descent parser producing an AST
#   codegen.a16  - Bytecode compiler emitting A16 VM instructions
#   vm.a16       - Stack-based interpreter executing bytecode
#   main.a16     - Entry point that ties it all together
#
# Usage:
#   a16 run bootstrap/main.a16
#
# The bootstrap compiler can compile simple A16 programs:
#   fn add(a, b):
#       return a + b
#   fn main():
#       println(add(2, 3))
